Explanation:
- `^` matches the start of the string.
- `\d+` matches one or more digits (0-9).
- `(.)` groups the next character to check if it''s a decimal point. If not, this part is ignored.
- `\.` matches a literal period (.)
- `\d+` matches one or more digits again. If there are no decimal places, this part is optional.

